# Environment
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Licensed and proprietary data (Layer 0, store, full-text, DuckDB)
# Per BUILD_PLAN §2.5: data never enters git
projects/*/raw/
projects/*/store/
projects/*/fulltext/

# A researcher's own project, ignored by default.
#
# Two reasons this is opt-in rather than opt-out. A query and its eligibility
# criteria describe an unpublished research direction, and someone running a
# review inside a clone of this repository should not publish their protocol by
# reflex on their first `git add -A`. And this repository is a tool, not a
# review: a project directory committed here is somebody's scratch work, which
# is how `projects/x/` -- an empty test artifact -- reached the v0.6.0 release.
#
# BUILD_PLAN §2.5 line 291 does recommend tracking `decisions.jsonl`, because it
# is irreplaceable human labour. Do that deliberately in your own repository:
#     git add -f projects/<slug>/decisions/decisions.jsonl \
#                projects/<slug>/criteria.yaml projects/<slug>/project.toml
projects/
*.duckdb
*.db

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
# Anchored to the repository root: an unanchored `lib/` would also ignore a future
# `src/prismabib/**/lib/`, silently dropping source from the commit.
/lib/
/lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
# (build outputs above are anchored below where they could shadow real source dirs)
pip-wheel-metadata/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

