# mypy
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json

# NOTE: do NOT ignore `.pre-commit-*` here. That glob matches
# `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, which MUST be tracked: it carries the §2.5 data guard,
# and on a public repo that guard is the gate that keeps licensed Scopus payloads out
# of an irreversible push. An ignored config means a fresh clone has no hooks at all.
# pre-commit's own cache lives in ~/.cache/pre-commit, outside the repository.

# mkdocs
site/
docs_build/

# mutmut (Stage 4). `mutmut run` copies the entire source tree and test suite into
# `mutants/` at the repository root and rewrites it in place. It is build output, but
# it does not look like build output in `git status` -- it looks like a second copy of
# the project, and committing it to a PUBLIC repo would publish a mutated `src/` that
# a reader could easily mistake for real code.
mutants/
.mutmut-cache

